IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`

-- ccc31-tests-periods.l4 -- tests for ccc31-forms-periods.l4: how a period that the Forms measure in years, months and days from a day is counted
-- (fork F16 of NOTES.md: the period begins ON the day named; `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` is the first day it no
-- longer covers). Expected values are hand-written: 30 days from 1 January are 1 to 30 January; `add months` clamps a day that does not exist.

§ `The first day after a period`

#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) EQUALS Date 31 1 2026
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 2 2026
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 1 2027
-- "two years less a day" (the core's `two years less a day`): from 1 January 2026 it covers up to 30 December 2027, so the first day after is 31 December 2027.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) `two years less a day` EQUALS Date 31 12 2027
-- A month from the 31st: the month has no such day, so the end clamps to the last day of February.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 31 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- A year from 29 February 2024: clamps to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 29 2 2024) (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- Months and days together: six months and ten days from 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 6, 10, FALSE) EQUALS Date 11 7 2026
-- A period of nothing ends where it begins.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026

§ `Whether a day falls within a period`

-- 30 days from 1 January 2026: the first day, the last day (30 January), the day after (31 January), the day before the start.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE)
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 30 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE))
-- A period of nothing covers no day.
#ASSERT NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE))
-- One year from 1 January 2026 covers 31 December 2026 and not 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE))
-- Across a leap day: 365 days from 1 January 2024 end on 30 December 2024 (2024 has 366 days), so 31 December 2024 is outside.
#ASSERT `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 30 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2024) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 365, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2024) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 365, FALSE))
